/-!
# Program 09: the chemiosmotic controversy on the real record (stress set)

Doc: `docs/programs/09-chemiosmosis-real-record.md`. Cases: `data/stress/09/cases.tsv`, CH-01 to
CH-49. Each case names the theorem or `#guard` below that pins what BioLean does today, so a later
change to the core that moves a verdict breaks a pin, visibly.

`BioLean/Examples/Chemiosmosis.lean` replays the controversy with six real papers and three
illustrative items. Here the illustrative items give way to the real record: 62 dated publications
(`data/stress/09/record.tsv`), 61 checked on Europe PMC and one (Ferguson 1985, no PMID) on
Crossref (`data/stress/09/references_checked.tsv`). 58 carry a direction and are encoded: 28 on
chemiosmosis (C), 11 on the chemical intermediate (S), 17 on Williams' localised coupling (W), 1 on
Green's conformational model (G), 1 on murburn (M). 4 are neutral and kept aside.

Two namespaces, kept apart on purpose:

* `BioLean.Stress.ChemiosmosisReal`: the record on the core as it is. No new rule, opinion
  operator or type. Encodings (single or dual entry, how reviews count, dropped items, weights,
  extra items such as the 1978 Nobel speech) are data. The one general lemma,
  `Rivalry.forall_from`, is about existing core functions.
* `BioLean.Proto.ChemiosmosisReal`: prototypes of the doc's options D1, F2, G, H, I, J, L and M.
  Some would change the core if adopted, some are curator encodings; each section says which.
  Nothing in the Stress part uses them.

Headline verdicts are `theorem ... := by decide +kernel`. Sweeps (leave one out, year scans, the
72-encoding grid) and printed numbers are `#guard`, evaluated by the interpreter. Numbers are
printed as `Rat.toDecimal` prints them: truncated to three decimals.

The record section between the two marker lines is generated by
`scripts/stress/chemiosmosis_emit.py` from `data/stress/09/record.tsv`.
-/

